Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

HatchLens is written in Go. The binary contains:

- the Go standard library, BSD-3-Clause license, Copyright The Go Authors;
- go-yaml, the YAML parser, MIT and Apache-2.0 licenses, see its repository;
- on Windows: golang.org/x/sys, BSD-3-Clause license, Copyright The Go
  Authors, and go-winio (named pipes), MIT license, Copyright Microsoft.

The HatchLens Host MSI contains hatchlens-wsl.tar, the root file system of a
temporary WSL distribution used by "hatchlens-host enable-quota": unmodified
packages of Alpine Linux 3.22 (among them BusyBox, musl, apk-tools and
e2fsprogs) under their own licenses, mostly GPL-2.0 and MIT, each listed in
/lib/apk/db/installed of the tar. Their source code is available from the
Alpine Linux project and, on request, from the maintainer.

The Linux container image is built FROM scratch and contains only the
HatchLens binary. The Windows image adds the binary to Microsoft's
nanoserver base image, which is under Microsoft's own license terms.
